A||||1||Wannabe||Sticking Throttle?||||4||
Z||000000||Wannabe||07-16-2001||10:35 AM||||Yesterday, during time trials at Mosport, I was on my final run of the day, and was improving considerably over my previous run. About half way through, I was approaching a corner, lifted to apply some brake before entering and the engine kept right on going! I hit the clutch and the revs shot right up to the redline. Obviously the throttle was stuck open, so I shut the car off. By this time, I was off the track so my run was ruined. As soon as the engine was re-starded, everything seemed fine. I checked the throttle springs and the linkage and there is no binding. Everything seems ok in normal driving. Is is possible that the IAC was stuck open? Anybody ever have something like this happen?||||reg||4
Z||000001||hyhy4u||07-16-2001||11:54 AM||||Yeah i had the throttle stick open once on my 87 GT..its kindof a funny story cause i got ahold of a police siren and i mounted it in the engine compartment..that night the throttle kept on sticking on me..pulled it out the next day and never happened again..guess the police gods where just tyring to tell me something..||||reg||1
